Subject: [PATCH] fix: add login/register flow and attach JWT to API requests

The backend now requires auth on /api/projects and /api/tasks (previous
commit), but the frontend never got a corresponding update - it kept
firing unauthenticated fetch() calls, which surfaced in the browser as
401s and an 'n.filter is not a function' crash from trying to array-map
an error response body.

- Add api.js: fetch wrapper that attaches the JWT and, on a 401 (missing/
  expired token), clears it and signals the app to fall back to login
  instead of crashing on the error payload
- Add AuthForm.jsx: login/register screen, toggles between the two modes
- App.jsx now gates on presence of a token; all data calls go through
  apiFetch instead of raw fetch()
- Fix index.html's <title> (was still the Vite default 'client')
